5,1,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I think we should focus on the actual problems we face daily, not just the flashy ideas.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,May,,"Agreed, Daisuke. Flashy ideas often ignore the humans doing the work. Let’s keep it grounded and practical.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Grounded is fine, but I’m tired of promises based on assumptions. We need to verify the actual constraints before committing to anything.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Ryuji,,Shunichi is right. We must verify constraints. I worry about where the money actually comes from before we commit to anything flashy.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Kenji,,I agree with Shunichi. We need to check the records of past rollouts to see what actually worked before we spend more money.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I’m a bit nervous, but I think we should look at the misrouted deliveries and the time lost copying records.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,May,,I’m curious about the staffing of the coordination group and how vendor queries are handled. Those seem like the real bottlenecks.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Shunichi,,I’m checking network coverage at customer plants and in-house developer availability. We keep promising dates based on access we don’t control.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Ryuji,,I will examine the capital budget and software allowance. I need to know the true source of funds before we discuss any other operational details.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Kenji,,I’ll check the outcomes of the last three internal rollouts and the record of cross-unit standardization efforts. I need to see if we’re repeating mistakes.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Daisuke,,I’m glad we’re looking at the real losses. I hope the data shows what I suspect about our daily struggles.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,May,,"I’m betting the coordination group is just a ghost. If they’re stretched thin, your “practical” ideas will just pile onto their already broken plates.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Shunichi,,"May, stop speculating. I’m verifying the actual access constraints. If the network is down, your coordination group is irrelevant.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Ryuji,,"Shunichi, your network check is valid, but it doesn’t answer my funding question. I need to know the budget source before we debate operational priorities.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Kenji,,"I’m not debating priorities yet. I’m just checking if we’ve already learned this lesson. If we keep repeating the same mistakes, the budget is wasted.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I just want to make sure we don’t ignore the small, daily frustrations. They add up to real losses.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,May,,"Daisuke, you’re right. Those small frustrations are exactly why I’m checking the staffing. If the rota breaks, who actually absorbs the extra work?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,Shunichi,,I’m not here to comfort anyone. I’m here to ensure we don’t promise dates we can’t keep. The network check is the only thing that matters right now.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I remain focused on the capital budget. Without knowing the true source of funds, operational debates are premature. I will wait for the data.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Kenji,,"I’m just waiting for the data. If the past three rollouts show the same failure pattern, we need to stop funding the same broken ideas.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
