35,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I found eleven misrouted deliveries and an hour daily lost to copying. These are real, measurable losses we ignore.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,May,,"Two people doing the work of ten. That’s not a bottleneck, it’s a structural failure. @Shunichi, your network is useless if no one is left to answer the phone.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"May, your staffing crisis doesn’t fix dead zones. Half the plants lose signal for afternoons, and device approval took six weeks. Your phone is useless if the network is down.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The capital line is frozen, but the software allowance has room. Per-head licences climb with every department added, while fixed-fee work has held steady for three years.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Ryuji, that’s good news. But my data shows broad tools get abandoned. We must fund narrow, single-trade solutions that actually stick.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Kenji, narrow tools help, but they don’t stop the copying. We need to fix the root cause of the duplication, not just the symptoms.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, you’re right. But fixing duplication won’t help if the same two people are drowning. We need to stop adding tasks to a broken rota.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, your rota is irrelevant if the signal is dead. Half the plants lose coverage for afternoons. Your phone is useless if the network is down.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Kenji, your narrow tools fit the frozen capital line. But per-head licences will spike next year. We must avoid that renewal trap.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Ryuji, agreed. We must avoid per-head traps. My data shows narrow tools survive because they have clear owners. We need to fund that specific, manageable scope.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, the copying loss is real. If we fix the duplication, maybe the rota pressure eases? I worry about adding more work to tired people.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, easing pressure isn’t the same as fixing it. If we don’t name who absorbs the extra work, the rota just breaks again.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, you’re still ignoring the physical reality. No amount of rota fixing helps if the signal is dead. I’m checking developer availability next.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, developer availability is secondary. The real risk is the renewal notice. We must secure a fixed-fee structure now to prevent next year’s budget shock.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Shunichi, I’m not ignoring the signal. I’m asking if we have the people to maintain it. My data shows tools fail without clear owners.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I’m quiet, but the data is clear. We lose an hour daily to copying. That’s a real, measurable loss we can’t ignore.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, you’re obsessed with signal, but I’m obsessed with people. If the rota breaks, your perfect network is just expensive silence.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, silence is better than a broken promise. My developers are locked until Q3, and the integrator left no docs. We can’t build on air.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,I will wait for the candidates. The fixed-fee structure is the only path that avoids the renewal trap.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"I’m ready for the candidates. My data proves narrow, owned tools survive. Let’s see if the proposals match that reality.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
